    "description": "For our client, a globally operating world market leader, we are currently seeking an experienced expert for\nGlobal STP Process Excellence & Lead Adoption (m/f/d)\n. As part of the \"Esphora\" program, you will support a comprehensive S/4HANA transformation to elevate source-to-pay processes to a new technological level and establish sustainable business excellence.\nStart:\nMid-April 2026\nDuration:\n6 months (with option for another 6 months)\nWork location:\nRemote (approx. 90%), occasional travel to locations in Germany (approx. 10%)\nImportant:\nAs the company language is English, your\nCV must be in English\n.\nOverview:\nIn this key role, you will act as the central orchestrator and \"first line of defense\" between system integrators, substream leads, and global end users. Your goal is to ensure the customer's digital sovereignty and translate complex process designs—from direct/indirect procurement to invoice-to-pay—into a lived global reality.\n\nSkills: Professional experience: Several years of very senior experience in STP processes, strategic purchasing or large-scale transformation programs., Project history: Proven success in Organizational Change Management (OCM) within complex ERP rollouts (ideally S/4HANA or SAP Ariba)., IT & process know-how: Sound understanding of the technical differences between PR and PO as well as confident handling of SAP environments for documentation creation., Methodological competence: Sovereignty in project management disciplines, stakeholder moderation and the creation of structured training curricula., Soft Skills: A high level of emotional intelligence and resilience to navigate safely in a global matrix environment., Language skills: Fluent English (C1/C2) is mandatory; German language skills are expressly advantageous due to the context., Willingness to travel: Flexibility for occasional business trips (approx. 10%) to locations such as clinics or factories in Germany.",
